#: piclo/data/practice.lua:28
msgid ""
"The top row says 5, and it has five squares: every one of them is filled. "
"Tap each square, or drag along the row."
msgstr ""

#: piclo/data/practice.lua:30
msgid "Rows 3 and 5 say 5 too. Fill them."
msgstr ""

#: piclo/data/practice.lua:32
msgid ""
"Row 2 says 1 1 1: three single squares with a gap between each. That takes "
"exactly five squares, so they only fit one way. Fill the three."
msgstr ""

#: piclo/data/practice.lua:34
msgid ""
"The gaps stay empty. Choose Cross in the toolbar and cross them, so you can "
"see the row is done."
msgstr ""

#: piclo/data/practice.lua:36
msgid "Row 4 is the same as row 2. Fill it to finish the picture."
msgstr ""

#: piclo/data/practice.lua:38
msgid ""
"Solved. Every puzzle works like this: find a line you can be sure of, mark "
"it, and move on."
msgstr ""

#: piclo/data/practice.lua:51
msgid "Rows 2 and 3 say 5. Fill them."
msgstr ""

#: piclo/data/practice.lua:53
msgid ""
"Column 3 says 4. Its run starts at the top or one square lower, and both "
"ways cover the middle three squares. Fill those."
msgstr ""

#: piclo/data/practice.lua:55
msgid "Columns 2 and 4 say 4 as well. Fill their middle three."
msgstr ""

#: piclo/data/practice.lua:57
msgid ""
"Row 4 says 3, and its run of three is there. The row is complete: cross its "
"other squares."
msgstr ""

#: piclo/data/practice.lua:59
msgid "Columns 1 and 5 say 2, and both have their two. Cross the rest of them."
msgstr ""

#: piclo/data/practice.lua:61
msgid ""
"Row 1 says 1 1, with three squares left. Two runs need a gap between them, "
"so they take the outer two. Fill those and cross the middle."
msgstr ""

#: piclo/data/practice.lua:63
msgid ""
"Finish the picture on your own. When you're stuck, the bulb in the toolbar "
"shows the next step."
msgstr ""

#: piclo/data/practice.lua:65
msgid ""
"Solved. That's all there is to it. The packs start small and grow from there."
msgstr ""

